# Universal Coding Rulebook — Pointer

This project follows the universal rulebook at:

`/Users/macbook/Github/vibeCodingRules/AGENTS.md`

Before any code change, the agent MUST:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` to determine which rule files apply to the task.
2. Run `feature-discovery.md` grilling (3–5 questions) unless a skip trigger fires.
3. Open every REQUIRED file from the routing matrix and skim mandatory sections.
4. Apply the per-edit checklist (sections A–H) to every line touched.
5. Sync `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` after any rule/cursor change (`cursor-sync.md`).

Hard bans (no exception without documented reason):

- Skipping REQUIRED files
- Guessing requirements when discovery is required
- Drive-by refactors outside the stated task
- New generic `utils` / `helpers` / `misc` modules
- `console.log` / debug prints in committed code
- A second pattern for something the codebase already does one way
- Caching auth/session responses; tokens in insecure client storage
- Bare verbs in REST URLs; skipping auth on protected handlers
